/security.txt /.well-known/security.txt 301

# Shortlinks. These are read off a screen — livestream lower thirds, slides,
# email — so they have to stay short and stay ours to repoint.
#
# 302, not 301: a permanent redirect gets cached by browsers and intermediaries,
# and the whole point of owning the shortlink is being able to change where it
# goes without chasing down every place it was already printed.
/discord https://discord.gg/puArEQHYN9 302
/discord/ https://discord.gg/puArEQHYN9 302

# /ph is deliberately NOT a static rule: its destination changes at go-live
# (before launch, Follow only exists on the discussion page; the upvote only
# appears on the product page once live). It is served by functions/ph.ts,
# which reads the same PH_GO_LIVE_MS as the rest of the site. This rule only
# normalises the trailing slash onto that Function.
/ph/ /ph 301
